17. Why the DP table is filled from right to left

                                Look at:                                
                                                palindrome[i][j]
                                
                                It depends on:                                
                                                palindrome[i + 1][j - 1]
                                
                                So the inner substring must already be computed.

                Therefore:                
                                for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--)
                
                        ensures that when we calculate:
                
                                palindrome[i][j]
                
                        the required:                
                                        palindrome[i+1][j-1]
                
                        is already available.

This is an example of dependency-driven DP traversal.
        Don't memorize "iterate backwards."

Instead ask:
                What state does my recurrence depend on, and in what order must those states be computed?

